    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0781" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg685"/>

                <head>No. 479.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peixotto to Mr. Hunter.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 12, 1872</date>. (Received March 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The consul of Germany has called to inform
                    me that he last evening received a telegram from Prince Bismarck, instructing
                    him to sign the note addressed to the Roumanian government concerning the
                    persecution of the. Israelites, copy of which I had the honor to inclose and
                    refer to in my dispatch No. 21, of the 9th instant.</p>
                <p>* * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c., &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BENJ. F. PEIXOTTO,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                            Consul.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
